   "source": [
    "{\n",
    " \"cells\": [\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"c00\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": \"# CaImAn vs our CNMFe — head-to-head on a synthetic movie\\n\\nRuns both pipelines on the same ground-truth synthetic 1p movie and compares:\\n\\n1. **Spatial recovery** — per-neuron Pearson r between each pipeline's `A` and the true footprints\\n2. **Temporal recovery** — per-neuron Pearson r between `C + YrA` (the noisy projected trace) and the true calcium trace\\n\\n`C + YrA` is used for the temporal comparison because it preserves the data's actual shape; OASIS-deconvolved `C` alone has small spike-timing distortions that drag Pearson down to ~0.85 even for a perfect extraction (see `tutorial2.ipynb` cell 26 for the why).\\n\\n**Prerequisites**: launch this notebook from a conda env that has CaImAn installed (e.g. `conda activate caiman_claude_nmfe; jupyter notebook`). The notebook just does `import caiman` — no local source-tree path hacks.\"\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"c01\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": \"import os, tempfile, time\\n\\nimport numpy as np\\nimport scipy.sparse as sp\\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\\n%matplotlib inline\\nplt.rcParams['figure.dpi'] = 120\",\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"c02\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 1. Generate the synthetic movie\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Same fixture as `tutorial2.ipynb` so results are directly comparable.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"c03\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"from tests.conftest import make_synthetic_movie\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"data = make_synthetic_movie(n_neurons=10, dims=(64, 64), T=6500,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                            noise_std=0.5, ar_decay=0.9, bg_strength=2.0, seed=55)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"movie    = data['movie']     # (T, H, W) float32\\n\",\n",
    "    \"A_true   = data['A_true']    # (H*W, K)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"C_true   = data['C_true']    # (K, T)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"centers  = data['centers']   # (K, 2)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"T, H, W  = movie.shape\\n\",\n",
    "    \"K        = C_true.shape[0]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f'Movie: {movie.shape}   neurons={K}   noise_std={data[\\\"sn_true\\\"]}   g_true={data[\\\"ar_decay\\\"]}')\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"c04\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 2. Helpers — Pearson, normalisation, neuron matching\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"`match_components_by_truth` pairs each true neuron with whichever extracted neuron has the highest spatial correlation, returning `(true_idx, est_idx, spatial_r)`. We use the same helper for both pipelines so the comparison is symmetric.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"c05\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"def pearson(a, b):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    a = a - a.mean(); b = b - b.mean()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    d = np.sqrt(np.sum(a ** 2) * np.sum(b ** 2))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    return float(np.dot(a, b) / d) if d > 0 else 0.0\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"def norm01(x):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    lo, hi = float(np.min(x)), float(np.max(x))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    return (x - lo) / (hi - lo + 1e-10)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"def match_components_by_truth(A_est, A_true_dense):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"\\\"\\\"Pair each true neuron with the extracted component that best matches it\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    spatially. Returns list of (true_idx, est_idx, spatial_r).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    A_e = np.asarray(A_est.todense() if sp.issparse(A_est) else A_est)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    A_t = A_true_dense\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    matches = []\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    if A_e.shape[1] == 0:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        return [(k, -1, 0.0) for k in range(A_t.shape[1])]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    for k_true in range(A_t.shape[1]):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        a_t = A_t[:, k_true]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        corrs = np.array([pearson(a_t, A_e[:, k]) for k in range(A_e.shape[1])])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        best = int(np.argmax(corrs))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        matches.append((k_true, best, float(corrs[best])))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    return matches\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"c06\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 3. Run our CNMFe pipeline\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"c07\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": \"from cnmfe.pipeline import CNMFe, CNMFeParams\\n\\nparams_ours = CNMFeParams(\\n    sigma=3.0,\\n    min_corr=0.8,\\n    min_pnr=6.0,\\n    n_iter_main=2,\\n    n_iter_temporal=2,\\n    mc_n_iter=1,\\n    spatial_max_thr=0.1,\\n    merge_thr_corr=0.85,\\n    merge_thr_overlap=0.5,\\n    global_ar=False,  # per-neuron g estimated from each C_raw[k]\\n    n_jobs=-1,\\n)\\n\\nt0 = time.time()\\nours = CNMFe(params_ours).fit(movie, do_motion_correction=False)\\nt_ours = time.time() - t0\\n\\nA_ours    = ours.A                            # (H*W, K) sparse\\nC_ours    = ours.C                            # (K, T)\\nYrA_ours  = ours.YrA                          # (K, T)\\nCproj_ours = C_ours + YrA_ours                # noisy projected trace\\n\\nprint(f'\\\\nours: K = {A_ours.shape[1]}   wall = {t_ours:.2f}s')\",\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"9daf973d\",\n",
    "   \"source\": \"# Iteration-equalised variant: same params but n_iter_main=1 to match CaImAn's\\n# hardcoded single-cycle structure. Isolates algorithm quality from iteration count.\\nparams_1iter = CNMFeParams(\\n    sigma=3.0, min_corr=0.8, min_pnr=6.0,\\n    n_iter_main=1,\\n    n_iter_temporal=2, mc_n_iter=1,\\n    spatial_max_thr=0.1, merge_thr_corr=0.85, merge_thr_overlap=0.5,\\n    global_ar=False,  # per-neuron g estimated from each C_raw[k]\\n    n_jobs=-1,\\n)\\nt0 = time.time()\\nours1 = CNMFe(params_1iter).fit(movie, do_motion_correction=False)\\nt_ours1 = time.time() - t0\\n\\nA_ours1   = ours1.A\\nC_ours1   = ours1.C\\nYrA_ours1 = ours1.YrA\\nCproj_ours1 = C_ours1 + YrA_ours1\\n\\nprint(f'\\\\nours (1 iter): K = {A_ours1.shape[1]}   wall = {t_ours1:.2f}s')\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"c08\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": \"## 4. Run CaImAn's CNMF-E pipeline — at its best\\n\\nCaImAn's CNMF-E entry point is `caiman.source_extraction.cnmf.CNMF` with\\n`method_init='corr_pnr'`, `p=1`, `nb=0`, `low_rank_background=None` — that disables the\\nrank-`gnb` global background and uses the ring model instead.\\n\\nRather than force *our* thresholds onto CaImAn, this notebook gives CaImAn the\\nconfiguration it is actually designed for, so the comparison reflects each pipeline at\\nits best:\\n\\n- **Patches** (`rf=32, stride=16`, `only_init=True`) — CaImAn's CNMF-E init and ring\\n  model were built to run on overlapping patches, not the whole FOV at once.\\n- **Background refinement** (`update_background_components=True`) — lets CaImAn refine its\\n  ring background during the fit. This is the single biggest driver of CaImAn's temporal\\n  quality here (without it, `C+YrA` against truth drops from ~0.97 to ~0.72 on the simple\\n  movie).\\n- **Thresholds tuned to CaImAn's own corr/pnr** (`tune_thresholds`) — we read CaImAn's\\n  `correlation_pnr` summary images and pick the most selective `(min_corr, min_pnr)` whose\\n  seed pool still covers ~8×K pixels, i.e. CaImAn's native operating point.\\n- **Footprints mapped to true `(h, w)` space** — CaImAn flattens `A` in Fortran order; for\\n  a square FOV that is a transpose of our C-order footprints. `detect_caiman_order`\\n  auto-detects and corrects it (otherwise the spatial-r comparison is artefactually low —\\n  ~0.63 instead of ~0.94 on the simple movie, purely from the transpose).\\n\\nThese choices are aligned with our model where CaImAn exposes an equivalent (`gSig=3`,\\n`merge_thr=0.85`, `ssub_B=1`, `ring_size_factor=1.5`, `thr_method='max', maxthr=0.1`,\\n`border_pix=5`). The remaining differences are **structural** (no configurable CaImAn\\nequivalent) and are catalogued in §9.\\n\\nCaImAn requires a memory-mapped movie file, so we save each movie to disk first. Outputs\\nland on `cnm.estimates`.\"\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"c09\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": \"import caiman as cm\\nfrom caiman.source_extraction.cnmf import cnmf as cnmf_module\\nfrom caiman.source_extraction.cnmf import params as params_module\\nfrom caiman.summary_images import correlation_pnr\\nfrom joblib.externals.loky import get_reusable_executor\\n\\n# --- CaImAn footprint orientation -----------------------------------------\\n# CaImAn flattens its A in Fortran order; our A / A_true use C order (np.ravel\\n# default). For a square FOV that difference is a transpose, which silently\\n# tanks the spatial-r comparison unless we map CaImAn's footprints back into\\n# true (h, w) C-order space. detect_caiman_order picks the reshape order whose\\n# footprint centroids best match the true centres (self-verifying).\\ndef _dense(A):\\n    return np.asarray(A.todense() if sp.issparse(A) else A)\\n\\ndef to_truth_space(A, dims, order):\\n    H, Wd = dims\\n    hw = _dense(A).reshape(H, Wd, -1, order=order)       # (H, W, K) in true space\\n    return hw.reshape(H * Wd, hw.shape[2], order='C')     # re-flatten consistently\\n\\ndef footprint_centroids(A, dims, order):\\n    H, Wd = dims\\n    hw = np.abs(_dense(A).reshape(H, Wd, -1, order=order))\\n    yy, xx = np.mgrid[0:H, 0:Wd]\\n    out = []\\n    for k in range(hw.shape[2]):\\n        img = hw[:, :, k]; s = img.sum()\\n        out.append((np.nan, np.nan) if s <= 0 else\\n                   (float((yy * img).sum() / s), float((xx * img).sum() / s)))\\n    return np.array(out)\\n\\ndef detect_caiman_order(A_caiman, dims, true_centers):\\n    best = None\\n    for order in ('F', 'C'):\\n        cents = footprint_centroids(A_caiman, dims, order)\\n        d = [np.sqrt(((true_centers - c) ** 2).sum(1)).min()\\n             for c in cents if np.isfinite(c[0])]\\n        md_ = float(np.mean(d)) if d else np.inf\\n        print(f'    order={order}: mean nearest-centroid dist to truth = {md_:5.2f} px')\\n        if best is None or md_ < best[1]:\\n            best = (order, md_)\\n    print(f'    -> using order={best[0]} for CaImAn footprints')\\n    return best[0]\\n\\n# --- CaImAn CNMF-E config + runner ----------------------------------------\\ndef caiman_cnmfe_opts(fname, *, fr=20.0, min_corr=0.8, min_pnr=6.0, decay_time=0.4):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Best-practice patch CNMF-E. Matched 1:1 to our CNMFeParams EXCEPT\\n    min_corr / min_pnr, which are tuned to CaImAn's own corr/pnr operating point\\n    (see tune_thresholds), plus the patch / background settings that let CaImAn\\n    run the way it is designed to: rf/stride patches, only_init refinement, and\\n    ring-background refinement (update_background_components=True).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    gSig = (3, 3); gSiz = (4 * gSig[0] + 1,) * 2\\n    return {\\n        'fnames': [fname], 'fr': fr, 'decay_time': decay_time,\\n        'method_init': 'corr_pnr', 'K': None, 'gSig': gSig, 'gSiz': gSiz,\\n        'merge_thr': 0.85, 'p': 1, 'tsub': 1, 'ssub': 1,\\n        'rf': 32, 'stride': 16, 'only_init': True,\\n        'nb': 0, 'nb_patch': 0, 'method_deconvolution': 'oasis',\\n        'low_rank_background': None, 'update_background_components': True,\\n        'min_corr': min_corr, 'min_pnr': min_pnr, 'normalize_init': False,\\n        'center_psf': True, 'ssub_B': 1, 'ring_size_factor': 1.5,\\n        'thr_method': 'max', 'maxthr': 0.1, 'del_duplicates': True, 'border_pix': 5,\\n    }\\n\\ndef tune_thresholds(images, K_expected, gSig=3, target_factor=8):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Pick the MOST selective (min_corr, min_pnr) from CaImAn's own corr/pnr\\n    images whose joint seed pool still covers ~target_factor x K pixels — i.e.\\n    CaImAn's native operating point rather than our thresholds forced onto it.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    cn, pnr = correlation_pnr(images, gSig=gSig, center_psf=True, swap_dim=False)\\n    c = cn.ravel(); p = pnr.ravel(); ok = np.isfinite(c) & np.isfinite(p); c, p = c[ok], p[ok]\\n    target = target_factor * K_expected\\n    chosen = None\\n    for mc in np.round(np.arange(0.50, 0.84, 0.02), 2)[::-1]:\\n        for mp in [12, 10, 8, 7, 6, 5, 4, 3]:\\n            if int(((c >= mc) & (p >= mp)).sum()) >= target:\\n                chosen = (float(mc), float(mp)); break\\n        if chosen: break\\n    if chosen is None:\\n        chosen = (0.50, 3.0)\\n    n = int(((c >= chosen[0]) & (p >= chosen[1])).sum())\\n    print(f'  tuned CaImAn min_corr={chosen[0]}, min_pnr={chosen[1]} '\\n          f'(seed pool {n} ~ {n / max(K_expected, 1):.1f}x K)')\\n    return chosen[0], chosen[1]\\n\\ndef save_as_memmap(mov, base):\\n    fname = cm.save_memmap([mov.astype(np.float32)], base_name=base, order='C')\\n    Yr, dims, Tm = cm.load_memmap(fname)\\n    return fname, Yr.T.reshape((Tm,) + dims, order='F')      # (T, H, W) view\\n\\ndef run_caiman(opts_dict, images, n_processes=1):\\n    get_reusable_executor().shutdown(wait=True)   # free joblib's loky pool first,\\n    opts = params_module.CNMFParams(params_dict=opts_dict)  # else setup_cluster trips\\n    c, dview, n_proc = cm.cluster.setup_cluster(\\n        backend='multiprocessing', n_processes=n_processes,\\n        single_thread=(n_processes == 1))\\n    try:\\n        t0 = time.time()\\n        cnm = cnmf_module.CNMF(n_processes=n_proc, dview=dview, Ain=None, params=opts)\\n        cnm.fit(images)             # mutates cnm in place; do NOT reassign\\n        dt = time.time() - t0\\n    finally:\\n        cm.cluster.stop_server(dview=dview)\\n    A = cnm.estimates.A\\n    C = np.asarray(cnm.estimates.C)\\n    YrA = np.asarray(cnm.estimates.YrA) if cnm.estimates.YrA is not None else np.zeros_like(C)\\n    return A, C, YrA, dt\\n\\n# --- Save the simple movie as a CaImAn-style memory-mapped file ------------\\nmmap_dir = tempfile.mkdtemp()\\nfname_mmap, images = save_as_memmap(movie, os.path.join(mmap_dir, 'caiman_movie_'))\\nprint(f'memmap: T={images.shape[0]}, dims={images.shape[1:]}, dir={mmap_dir}')\",\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"06dd646e\",\n",
    "   \"source\": \"### Parameter correspondence table\\n\\n| Our `CNMFeParams` | CaImAn param | Value | Status |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| `sigma=3.0` | `gSig=(3,3)` | 3 | ✓ matched |\\n| `ar_order=1` | `p` | 1 | ✓ matched |\\n| `ring_size_factor=1.5` | `ring_size_factor` | 1.5 | ✓ matched |\\n| `border_px=5` | `border_pix` | 5 | ✓ matched |\\n| `center_psf=True` | `center_psf` | True | ✓ matched |\\n| `merge_thr_corr=0.85` | `merge_thr` | 0.85 | ✓ matched (temporal corr threshold) |\\n| `spatial_max_thr=0.1` | `thr_method='max', maxthr=0.1` | 0.1 | ✓ matched |\\n| full-res ring bg | `ssub_B=1` | 1 | ✓ matched |\\n| `min_corr` / `min_pnr` | `min_corr` / `min_pnr` | *tuned per movie* | + CaImAn-tuned — set to CaImAn's own corr/pnr operating point via `tune_thresholds`, not forced to ours |\\n| — | `rf=32, stride=16` | patches | + CaImAn best-practice — CNMF-E is designed to run in patches |\\n| — | `only_init=True` | — | + CaImAn best-practice — standard patch-init refinement |\\n| ring bg refined in BCD | `update_background_components=True` | True | + CaImAn best-practice — biggest temporal-quality driver |\\n| C-order footprints | Fortran-order `A` → mapped to true space | — | + orientation auto-corrected (`detect_caiman_order`) |\\n| `n_iter_main=2` | *(CaImAn's patch refinement schedule)* | — | ⚠ structural — different refinement loop |\\n| `merge_thr_overlap=0.5` (Jaccard) | *any pixel overlap > 0* | — | ⚠ structural — CaImAn has no Jaccard threshold |\\n| `merge_centre_dist_factor=2.0` | *(no equivalent)* | — | ⚠ structural — no centre-distance merge fallback |\\n| `init_min_corr_neuron` / `init_max_corr_bg` / `seed_suppress_factor` | *(no direct param)* | — | ⚠ structural — CaImAn init uses different internal thresholds |\\n\\n`+` = changed to give CaImAn its best shot; `⚠` = structural difference with no configurable\\nfix. The structural items in §9 are what remains after CaImAn is run at its best.\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {}\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"c10\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": \"# --- Run CaImAn on the simple movie (best-practice config) -----------------\\n# Thresholds are tuned to CaImAn's OWN corr/pnr operating point, then footprints\\n# are mapped back into true (h, w) space with the auto-detected reshape order.\\nprint('Tuning CaImAn thresholds from its own corr/pnr (simple movie):')\\nmc, mp = tune_thresholds(images, K_expected=K)\\n\\nA_caiman_raw, C_caiman, YrA_caiman, t_caiman = run_caiman(\\n    caiman_cnmfe_opts(fname_mmap, fr=20.0, min_corr=mc, min_pnr=mp), images)\\nCproj_caiman = C_caiman + YrA_caiman\\n\\nprint('Detecting CaImAn footprint order (simple):')\\ntrue_cents = footprint_centroids(A_true, (H, W), 'C')\\nCAIMAN_ORDER = detect_caiman_order(A_caiman_raw, (H, W), true_cents)\\nA_caiman = to_truth_space(A_caiman_raw, (H, W), CAIMAN_ORDER)   # (H*W, K), C-order\\n\\nprint(f'\\\\ncaiman: K = {A_caiman.shape[1]}   wall = {t_caiman:.2f}s')\",\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# cm.stop_server(\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# )\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"id\": \"85d69a6fca1241d8\",\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"c11\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 5. Spatial recovery — `A` vs `A_true`\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"For each true neuron we pick whichever extracted component matches it best, then report the spatial Pearson r between those flat footprints. A score above ~0.7 means the extracted footprint genuinely covers the true neuron.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"c12\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": \"matches_ours   = match_components_by_truth(A_ours,   A_true)\\nmatches_ours1  = match_components_by_truth(A_ours1,  A_true)\\nmatches_caiman = match_components_by_truth(A_caiman, A_true)\\n\\nrs_A_ours   = np.array([m[2] for m in matches_ours])\\nrs_A_ours1  = np.array([m[2] for m in matches_ours1])\\nrs_A_caiman = np.array([m[2] for m in matches_caiman])\\n\\nfp_ours   = A_ours.shape[1]   - (rs_A_ours   > 0.7).sum()\\nfp_ours1  = A_ours1.shape[1]  - (rs_A_ours1  > 0.7).sum()\\nfp_caiman = A_caiman.shape[1] - (rs_A_caiman > 0.7).sum()\\n\\nprint(f'                      ours(2)   ours(1)    caiman')\\nprint(f'K extracted           {A_ours.shape[1]:6d}    {A_ours1.shape[1]:6d}    {A_caiman.shape[1]:6d}')\\nprint(f'mean spatial r        {rs_A_ours.mean():6.3f}    {rs_A_ours1.mean():6.3f}    {rs_A_caiman.mean():6.3f}')\\nprint(f'min  spatial r        {rs_A_ours.min():6.3f}    {rs_A_ours1.min():6.3f}    {rs_A_caiman.min():6.3f}')\\nprint(f'recovered (>0.7)      {(rs_A_ours > 0.7).sum():4d}/{K}    {(rs_A_ours1 > 0.7).sum():4d}/{K}    {(rs_A_caiman > 0.7).sum():4d}/{K}')\\nprint(f'unmatched FP          {fp_ours:6d}    {fp_ours1:6d}    {fp_caiman:6d}')\\nprint()\\nprint('Per-neuron spatial r:')\\nprint(f'  true   ours(2)  ours(1)  caiman')\\nfor k in range(K):\\n    print(f'   {k:2d}    {rs_A_ours[k]:.3f}    {rs_A_ours1[k]:.3f}    {rs_A_caiman[k]:.3f}')\",\n",
