    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"4d74449a\",\n",
    "   \"source\": \"## 9. Known limitations of this comparison\\n\\nCaImAn is now run **at its best** (patches + ring-background refinement, thresholds tuned to\\nits own corr/pnr operating point) and its footprints are compared in true `(h, w)` space with\\nan auto-detected, centroid-verified reshape order — so the earlier artefacts (forced\\nthresholds, transposed footprints, starved background) are gone. The numbers above should\\nstill be read with these remaining caveats in mind.\\n\\n**1. `evaluate_components` is not called** on either side — raw output vs raw output.\\nCaImAn ships a CNN + SNR + spatial-correlation quality filter\\n(`cnm.estimates.evaluate_components`); on real data it is CaImAn's main precision advantage\\n(it rejects ghost cells, split neurons, low-SNR components). Omitting it inflates CaImAn's\\nfalse-positive count here.\\n\\n**2. Spatial-solve normalisation.** CaImAn passes traces through\\n`StandardScaler(with_mean=False)` before LassoLars; our `update_spatial` uses raw traces.\\nWhen amplitudes vary widely across neurons, CaImAn's normalisation reduces the chance a\\nbright component over-shadows a dim one during pixel assignment.\\n\\n**3. AR(1) decay strategy.** CaImAn estimates `g` per neuron per iteration; we estimate `g`\\nonce from `C_raw` per neuron (`global_ar=False`) and cache it (no fudge-factor drift). The\\nrealistic movie now uses GCaMP8m for every cell, so the true `g` is concentrated near\\n`g`≈0.76 (τ≈180 ms at 20 fps) with only a small per-neuron spread — a *known* target you can\\ncheck each pipeline's recovered `g` against (`decay_time_from_g` in `cnmfe.temporal`). When\\nthe indicator decay is known, setting `decay_time_ms`+`frame_rate_hz` on `CNMFeParams` shrinks\\nour Yule-Walker estimate toward the physical `g` (Bayesian prior).\\n\\n**4. Refinement loop.** Our model runs `n_iter_main` full spatial→temporal→merge cycles with\\nOASIS from the start; CaImAn's patch pipeline (`only_init=True`) has its own\\ninit→merge→refine schedule with a `p=0` then `p=1` temporal phase. The loops are not\\nstep-for-step identical.\\n\\n**5. No real-recording validation** — synthetic data only. A synthetic-data gap need not\\ntransfer to real recordings, in either direction; CaImAn is extensively validated on real 1p\\ndata and ours is not.\\n\\n**6. Background model** — even the realistic simulator's background is a sum of separable\\nrank-1 components, simpler than real neuropil / blood-vessel / hemodynamic structure that\\nneither the ring model nor the simulator captures.\",\n",
